'name'>Month</td><td class='unit'>mon</td><td class='rval'>               10 </td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class='ndesc' id='d_11_7' >#7</td><td class='desc'>0 04 003</td><td class='name'>Day<\n--- getbufr help (text)\n\n Getbufr help\n This site uses third part cookies. If you navigate in these pages we assume you accept its use.\n Learn more\n Got it!\n -->\n Professional information about meteorological conditions in the world\n OGIMET\n OGIMET\n Versión española\n WEATHER MODEL FORECAST\n G FS world weather maps\n METEOGRAMS\n G ramet a ero\n G ramet m eteo\n INDEXES\n Q uery about indexes\n UNDECODED REPORTS\n S ynop reports\n S ynop by countries\n L atest synops\n M etar/Taf reports\n L atest metar\n L atest Taf\n U pper air soundings\n S oundings by countries\n TEXT INFORMATION\n D aily summaries\n C ountry summaries\n W eather ranking\n G SOD Daily summaries\n C LIMAT monthly summaries\n BUFR REPORTS\n G et B ufr reports\n GRAPHIC INFORMATION\n O penmaps data navigation\n S ynops over countries\n W orld synop navigation\n M etars over countries\n W orld metar navigation\n W orld GSOD data navigation\n OTHER\n D atabase state\n C redits\n L icense\n O gimet news\n W MO Resolution 40\n D ocumentation\n C ontact\n Advertisements\n getbufr\n getbufr.php Is a small php application to get BUFR files and lists from Ogimet Database.\n The URL is\n http://www.ogimet.com/getbufr.php\n To work with getbufr.php you need to add some GET arguments to URL:\n 1) The type of result to get, i.e. a list with selected BUFR files or a tar file with all the selected files. To select add the argument 'res'. The available values are 'list' or 'tar'. This is not mandatory. Default is to get a list of files. See the examples.\n 2) Time interval selection. This is mandatory. You can select by date/time collected in GTS or by date/time of bulletin.\nTo select begin and end of date/time collected in GTS use arguments 'beg_gts' and 'end_gts'. To select by nominal date/time in bulletin headers use 'beg' and 'end'.\nIn all cases the date/time format is YYYYMMDDhhmm UTC.\n As example, to get a tar file with BUFR collected in NOAA GTS gateway between 06:00 and 06:15 UTC (both included) on January 30 2017:\n http://www.ogimet.com/getbufr.php?res=tar&beg_gts=201701300600&end_gts=201701300615\n To get a list of BUFR files with nominal bulletin header equal to 06:00 UTC on January 29 2017 (note that the begin and end date/time are the same)\n http://www.ogimet.com/getbufr.php?res=list&beg=201701290600&end=201701290600\n 3) Selection by emisor center. This is optional. The default is all centers. Argument used is 'ecenter' and the values are a four letters center index.\nAs example, to get a tar file with BUFR files released by emisor center LEMM with bulletin header at 12:00 UTC on 6 January 2017:\n http://www.ogimet.com/getbufr.php?res=tar&beg=201701061200&end=201701061200&ecenter=LEMM\n 4) Selection by report type. This is optional. Default is all types. The argument is 'type' and the values used is to match first characters of WMO T1T2A1A2ii designators.\nAll BUFR have T1 = 'I' and then all type values used must begin with 'I'. Read below about the meaning of T1T2A1A2ii designators.\n As example, for BUFR with 'surface/sea level' observations T2='S' thus if we just want this kind of BUFR in prior example\n http://www.ogimet.com/getbufr.php?res=tar&beg=201701061200&end=201701061200&ecenter=LEMM&type=IS\n 5) Finally it is possible to get directly a file if we know its name. Argumet is 'file' and the value is the filename. As example\n http://www.ogimet.com/getbufr.php?file=20170129083121_ISSH01_LFPW_290800.bufr\n You must read below about the filename format of bufr files in Ogimet database.\n And what's about quota limits?. At the moment it is limite\n--- getbufr list guess\n<h1>403 Forbidden</h1>\nhttp=403\n",
